        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Bowdoin College, Brown University, WBOR\n- Places: Maine, Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Providence, Rhode Island, United States, English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations, Brunswick\n- Topics: university founding and chartering, colonial colleges, radio stations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1764, Brown University was founded as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.\n- Brown University is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\n- In 1794, when Bowdoin College was chartered, Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.\n- WBOR is a radio station at 91.1 FM licensed to Bowdoin College in Brunswick, Maine, United States.",
